    "encoding_note": "SENT encodes each 4-bit nibble as a single-wire pulse of (12 + value) ticks, measured falling-edge to falling-edge. A frame is a 56-tick synchronization/calibration pulse, a status nibble, 1-6 data nibbles, and a 4-bit CRC nibble, with an optional pause pulse. The slow serial channel (Short/Enhanced Serial Message) rides in bit 2/3 of the status nibble."
